    "Type": "ContractGeneratorHandler_List",
    "MissionType": {
        "UUID": "8251b278-ffc5-49e2-8cea-2ffa8007e4a1",
        "Name": "Resource Drive - Hurston"
    },
    "MissionGiver": "Hurston Dynamics",
    "Title": "RESOURCE DRIVE: SMALL CARGO RETRIEVAL",
    "TitleKey": "GoblinG_Hurston_RecoverCargo_S_Title",
    "Description": "HURSTON DYNAMICS OUTSOURCING\nCONTRACT: Resource Drive\nOUTSOURCE MANAGER: A. Carmichael\nRISK ASSESSMENT: Moderate\n\nAccording to our trackers, an important shipment of cargo appears to have stopped moving over at <EM4>~mission(Location|Address)</EM4>.\n\nThe pilot isn\u2019t answering, so we assume they\u2019ve been compromised. My superiors have written this off as a loss, but if any of the materials can be recovered, we are prepared to compensate you. Any standard <EM4>tractor beam</EM4> should be fine to facilitate the transfer of cargo to your ship after any hostile ships have been dealt with. Expect to find between <EM4>50-55 SCU</EM4> of various box sizes.\n\nBring what you find to a freight elevator at: <EM4>~mission(Destination|Address|ListAll)</EM4>. I\u2019ll send a member of our team to inspect them.\n\nIf the abandoned vessel is still intact, and you have an available pilot with you, you could avoid having to transfer that cargo and just fly it back.\n\n\n** The information transmitted may contain confidential and/or privileged material. Any review, retransmission, dissemination or other use of or taking action in reliance upon this information by persons or entities other than the intended recipient is prohibited. **",
    "DescriptionKey": "GoblinG_Hurston_RecoverCargo_S_Desc",
    "DisplayDescription": "HURSTON DYNAMICS OUTSOURCING\nCONTRACT: Resource Drive\nOUTSOURCE MANAGER: A. Carmichael\nRISK ASSESSMENT: Moderate\n\nAccording to our trackers, an important shipment of cargo appears to have stopped moving over at <EM4>[Location|Address]</EM4>.\n\nThe pilot isn\u2019t answering, so we assume they\u2019ve been compromised. My superiors have written this off as a loss, but if any of the materials can be recovered, we are prepared to compensate you. Any standard <EM4>tractor beam</EM4> should be fine to facilitate the transfer of cargo to your ship after any hostile ships have been dealt with. Expect to find between <EM4>50-55 SCU</EM4> of various box sizes.\n\nBring what you find to a freight elevator at: <EM4>Lorville</EM4>. I\u2019ll send a member of our team to inspect them.\n\nIf the abandoned vessel is still intact, and you have an available pilot with you, you could avoid having to transfer that cargo and just fly it back.\n\n\n** The information transmitted may contain confidential and/or privileged material. Any review, retransmission, dissemination or other use of or taking action in reliance upon this information by persons or entities other than the intended recipient is prohibited. **",
